 "text": "Hi! How are you today? Use dry tinder, like dry leaves, or small twigs, at the bottom. Then build up with larger stuff, like dead branches, so it doesn't blow out. They' amazing. Roll them up, and they light with a spark. Wrap them in dry leaves and you can use them again. Keep it small to start, about the size of your palm. Then a good sized pan is enough. A bigger fire is only useful if you have a lot of fuel. Put it as far away from your tent as you can reach, and never sleep directly under tree.",
